  "rounds": {
    "1": {
      "note": "In everyday Cantonese an adjective usually comes after 好 (hou2, very) even when you just mean “is”: 好大 (hou2 daai6) = “(is) big”. Make it negative with 唔 (m4, not) in front — 唔大 (m4 daai6) = “not big”; and use 太 (taai3) for “too…” — 太貴 (taai3 gwai3) = “too expensive”.",
